** The crust and mantle are solid rock with appreciable rigidity and moderate density. The outer core is liquid, so it has no rigidity at all, and the inner core is solid, very rigid and very dense. S waves are shear waves and require a medium that can sustain a shear stress, so they travel through the solid mantle and the solid inner core but their velocity falls to zero in the liquid outer core. P waves are compressional and travel through both solids and liquids, so they are present at every depth, and their speed rises and falls with the changes in rigidity and density at each boundary.
v_s = \sqrt{\frac{\mu}{\rho}}
**
